ot even the  true  cost of this tragedy this is the  chemotherapy questions  that um you all asked me kelly russell's  is another life taken last year but a  young mother did not die of covert 19  she had stage 4 bowel cancer the number  of people who are going to be dying from  cancer  is is now accelerating this is costing  people's lives  her devastated father craig told me  kelly might still be alive today  if her cancer treatment had not been  stopped  a basic mindset at that time was that  to her the chemotherapy was keeping her  alive  when you're 31 years old and you've got  a six-year-old son  every day is precious one hundred  thousand  lives gone that's more than the  population  of this city all lost  in just 12 months and these  are the lives taken directly by covert  the real tragedy is much  much greater ashish joshi sky news  bath
 

